# MapStruct Enum Conversion - CRITICAL

**MapStruct cannot automatically convert enum types to String/primitive types.**

When mapping enum fields to different target types (enum → String, enum → int, etc.), you MUST explicitly provide a conversion method.

## Required Pattern

```java
@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")
public interface MyMapper {

  TargetDto toDto(Entity entity);

  // Always add explicit enum conversion method
  default String statusToString(EnumStatus status) {
    if (status == null) {
      return null;
    }
    return status.name();
  }
}
```

## Why This Matters

- MapStruct generates implementations at **compile-time** via annotation processor
- Without explicit conversion methods, the processor cannot determine how to convert enums
- **Silent failure**: Compilation succeeds, but implementation is NOT generated
- **Runtime error**: `Mappers.getMapper()` throws `ClassNotFoundException: Cannot find implementation for YourMapper`
- **Test failure**: Tests mysteriously fail with "method not found" errors when calling mapper

## Solution Checklist

- ✅ Add `default` method for every enum-to-String/primitive mapping
- ✅ Handle null inputs safely (return `null` if input is `null`)
- ✅ Use `status.name()` to convert enum to String
- ✅ After writing: verify `MapperImpl.class` exists in `target/classes/`
- ✅ If MapperImpl missing: recompile with `mvn clean compile -pl {module}`
